 ## Background
-Oriented Gaussian Splatting was introduced in "From Blobs to Spokes: High-Fidelity Surface Reconstruction via Oriented Gaussians" [S1]. It addresses the lack of reciprocity in standard 3D Gaussian Splatting attenuation, which prevents the direct application of the Objects as Volumes (OaV) framework for deriving explicit geometric fields [S1]. The method builds on the OaV theory [39] and integrates with differentiable rasterizers [55, 56, 57].
+Oriented Gaussian Splatting was introduced in "From Blobs to Spokes: High-Fidelity Surface Reconstruction via Oriented Gaussians" [S1]. It addresses the lack of reciprocity in standard 3D Gaussian Splatting attenuation, which prevents the direct application of the Objects as Volumes (OaV) framework for deriving explicit geometric fields [S1]. The method builds on the OaV theory [39] and integrates with differentiable rasterizers [55, 56, 57] [S1].
 
